(* The package i2c: transactions with the registers of devices on the I2C bus
   Wire of the board, for devices without a package of their own. Grades:
   time-interval-rational, in milliseconds.

   A device is given by its 7-bit address and a register by its 8-bit
   address. I2cWriteN (device, register, value) writes the value, modulo
   2^N, as an unsigned big-endian integer of N bits to the registers from the
   given one on; I2cReadN (device, register) reads one. A larger device or
   register address, or a transaction the device does not acknowledge, is a
   run-time error. The default implementations take the time of the
   transaction and read zeros.

   PROVISIONAL: the bounds of the running times are estimates for a bus of
   100 to 400 kHz, to be measured on the device. *)

operation I2cWrite8 : nat * nat * nat ~> unit # [0, 2]
default I2cWrite8 _ = delay 1/10

operation I2cWrite16 : nat * nat * nat ~> unit # [0, 2]
default I2cWrite16 _ = delay 1/10

operation I2cWrite32 : nat * nat * nat ~> unit # [0, 2]
default I2cWrite32 _ = delay 1/10

operation I2cRead8 : nat * nat ~> nat # [0, 2]
default I2cRead8 _ = delay 1/10; 0

operation I2cRead16 : nat * nat ~> nat # [0, 2]
default I2cRead16 _ = delay 1/10; 0

operation I2cRead32 : nat * nat ~> nat # [0, 2]
default I2cRead32 _ = delay 1/10; 0
